diff --git a/docs/implementation.md b/docs/implementation.md
index 3016897..d8643e1 100644
--- a/docs/implementation.md
+++ b/docs/implementation.md
@@ -5,3 +5,4 @@
 - A question stores its ordered options as a JSON array of `{ "text": "…", "correct": true }` objects. The form retains its raw submitted rows separately, so empty rows and their checkboxes can be rendered again on a failed validation without changing the saved question.
 - Questions have a unique position within their quiz. Appends and adjacent swaps run in a transaction; gaps left by deletions do not affect ordering. Inactive questions retain their place and are filtered out only for preview.
 - Preview renders a snapshot of the current active questions and uses in-page JavaScript state for progress and scoring. It has no submission endpoint and does not write answers to cookies, browser storage, or the database. For a future public game, don't send unrevealed answers to players as this moderator-only preview does.
+- Quiz JSON is a content-only format, independent of database IDs and timestamps. `Quiz#export_contents` lists the exact fields to expose, including inactive questions in position order. `QuizImport` checks the JSON types (including boolean flags), inserts questions in array order, and reuses the question form's option normalization and model validations. A single transaction rolls back the new quiz and all of its questions on an error.
